{"B_expression":"-1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))**2)","C_expression":"-1/2","derivation":"Retain the active parent program unchanged. The residual algebra confirms the observed behavior is exactly the expected next-order term.\n\nWith g = r/2 + delta where delta = r^2*B + u*r*C (inside chi support), the full residual expands as:\nE = 2(1+u)g + g^2 - r = [2r^2B + r^2/4 + r^3B + r^4B^2] + ur + 2u*delta + r*delta_u + delta_u^2 + 2*delta_r*delta_u\n\nThe bracketed pure remainder vanishes identically (verified by substituting B = -1/(2(1+sqrt(1+r))^2) and simplifying to 0). With C = -1/2, the leading ur term cancels: the ur contribution from the 2(1+u)g expansion is +ur, and from 2u*delta_u = 2u*(ur*(-1/2)) = -ur, giving 0.\n\nThe dominant remaining term is -u^2*r (from 2u*delta_u = 2u*(-ur/2)), which is structural to the two-slot correction form and cannot be eliminated by any choice of B(r,u), C(r,u) since no u^2*r slot exists in the correction r^2*B + ur*C. Numerical confirmation: UNIFORM row x=1/8 s=0 has u=0.007782, r=0.0001929, predicted -u^2*r = -1.17e-8, observed residual = -1.19e-8. The small discrepancy is from the subdominant terms 2ur^2B - ur^2/2 ~ -1e-10.\n\nAll other in-support rows show the same O(u^2*r) scaling. Rows with |u|>1/4 or |r|>1/2 are outside chi support and correctly receive only the linear g=r/2 (e.g., LEFT x=1/8 s=0: u=-0.5, residual=0.1405 matches 0.375^2-0=0.140625). Both bodies are C-infinity on r>-1 (open neighborhood of the evaluation rectangle |r|<1/2); sqrt(1+r)>0 throughout, no branch points or singularities.","inspect":[],"note":"Program retained from P03_W0. The ~1e-8 residuals in UNIFORM/LEFT in-support rows are the irreducible O(u^2*r) term of the two-slot covariance quotient, not a failure. No further reduction is possible within the fixed r^2*B + ur*C correction structure. A successor should: (1) verify that as stages progress and z drifts further from 1, the fraction of points falling outside chi_u support (|u|>1/4) grows, reducing the number of points receiving the quadratic correction; (2) note that the LEFT/RIGHT/BOTH edge-source families already produce |u| values up to 0.5 at t=1/64, meaning those points are permanently outside u-support and will always show O(r)-sized residuals from the linear reference; (3) the r=-1 LEFT row (target=0, z=1) is permanently outside r-support (|r|=1>1/2) and will always show residual (1+g)^2 - 0 with g=r/2=-0.5, giving 0.25. None of these are errors. No analytic-domain certificate is issued; smoothness rests on the explicit algebraic form. This is a local coefficient-field construction for the fixed two-slot quotient."}